    [Doc][Misc] Reorganize and refine EPLB documentation structure (#20086)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This PR reorganizes and refines the Expert Parallelism Load Balancer
    (EPLB) documentation to improve readability and structure. Specifically,
    it:
    - Renames the "Overview" section to "Feature Introduction" and
    integrates the benefits directly into it.
    - Moves and renames "Usage Recommendations" to "Usage Scenarios" for
    better flow.
    - Converts several sub-headers to proper heading levels (e.g., changing
    `###` to `####` for weight formats and hardware constraints).
    - Renames "How to Use EPLB" to "Feature Usage".
    - Fixes minor formatting and indentation issues in the "Critical
    Considerations" section.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is a documentation-only update.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Documentation changes were verified locally to ensure correct rendering.
    
